Continuing the tradition since 1999 when Dell began factory-installing
Red Hat Linux on all PowerEdge Servers, Dell is pleased to announce
availability of the PowerEdge 7150 Intel Itanium-based server, running
Red Hat Linux 7.1 for the Itanium Processor.

For further information on the PowerEdge 7150, see
http://www.dell.com/us/en/esg/topics/esg_pedge_rackmain_servers_1_pedge_7150
.htm.
Systems may be ordered today over the phone or through your Dell sales
representative. 

For further information on Dell's Linux system offerings, including our
whole line of PowerEdge Servers and select Precision workstations,
Inspiron and Latitude notebooks, and Dimension desktops,
see http://www.dell.com/linux.


Dell PowerEdge 7150
 
The PowerEdge 7150 delivers the performance of 64-bit computing with Intel
Itanium processors and leverages the strengths of Dell's direct model to
deliver affordable enterprise class solutions.

